    "result_text": "The full build passes green. \n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `ownerSegment` derived field on the owner API.\n\n**Spec:** `ownerSegment` = `<TIER>_<AREA>` \u2014 TIER is `PREMIUM` when `membershipLevel` \u2265 3 else `STANDARD`; AREA is `METRO` when `locality` is a known region (NSW/VIC/QLD) else `REGIONAL`.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added an `ownerSegment` property to the `Owner` schema (a read-only string enum of the four allowed values), so the code generator produces `OwnerDto.OwnerSegmentEnum` and the field appears in the response.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a `@Mapping` for `ownerSegment` plus an `ownerSegment(Owner)` default method that reuses the existing `membershipLevel(owner)` and `locality(owner)` derivations to build the segment, following the same pattern as the other derived fields.\n\nThe two acceptance tests (`STANDARD_METRO` for a Sydney/NSW owner, `STANDARD_REGIONAL` for an unknown-region owner) pass, and the full suite is green (`Tests run: 2, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`, BUILD SUCCESS).",
